In '''EvilQuest''', skills define a character's capabilities, determining their efficiency in combat, resource harvesting, artisan manufacturing, and wilderness navigation. As players perform actions related to a specific skill, they earn [[Experience|experience points (XP)]], advancing their skill level from its starting level up to the maximum level cap of '''150'''.

There are currently '''16 skills''' in the game, categorized into five core disciplines: Combat, Magic, Gathering, Artisan, and Support.

== Key Mechanics ==
* '''Maximum Skill Level''': Every skill on EvilQuest can be trained up to a maximum of '''Level 150'''.
* '''Total Level Cap''': With 16 skills, the maximum achievable total level is '''2,400''' (16 skills &times; 150).
* '''Experience Progression''': Reaching level 150 requires '''2,033,749,558 XP'''. The cumulative experience curve follows an exponential formula where required XP roughly doubles every 7 levels. See the full progression table on the [[Experience]] page.
* '''Engine Hard Cap''': Beyond level 150, players can continue gaining XP until hitting the absolute 32-bit signed integer limit of '''2,147,483,647 XP''' (<math>2^{31} - 1</math>). The ultimate account XP cap across all 16 skills is '''34,359,738,352 XP'''.
* '''Starting Skill Levels''':
** [[Hitpoints]] begins at '''Level 10''' with '''1,154 XP'''.
** [[Light Magic]] and [[Dark Magic]] begin at '''Level 0''' with '''0 XP'''.
** All other 13 skills begin at '''Level 1''' with '''0 XP'''.
* '''[[Combat Level]]''': A composite martial rating (ranging from '''Level 3''' to '''Level 172''') calculated deterministically from seven combat-related skills: [[Defence]], [[Hitpoints]], [[Weaponry]], [[Strength]], [[Ranging]], [[Light Magic]], and [[Dark Magic]].

