== [[Combat Skills]] ==
Combat skills govern a character's offensive power, defensive resilience, and survivability in battle against both monsters and other players.

* [[File:Weaponry.png|21x21px|middle|link=Weaponry|alt=Weaponry]] '''[[Weaponry]]''': Governs melee accuracy and sets level requirements for equipping weapons, ranging from basic Bronze daggers to end-game Vorass blades.
* [[File:Strength.png|21x21px|middle|link=Strength|alt=Strength]] '''[[Strength]]''': Directly increases maximum damage roll (max hit) in melee combat. Higher Strength lets you deal devastating blows to opponents.
* [[File:Defence.png|21x21px|middle|link=Defence|alt=Defence]] '''[[Defence]]''': Reduces enemy hit chance and mitigates incoming physical damage. Sets requirements for equipping tier armor from Bronze up to Crimsonite and Vorass.
* [[File:Ranging.png|21x21px|middle|link=Ranging|alt=Ranging]] '''[[Ranging]]''': Governs accuracy and damage with ranged weapons (shortbows, longbows, arrows). Also determines equip requirements for Leather and Dragonhide armor sets.
* [[File:Hitpoints.png|21x21px|middle|link=Hitpoints|alt=Hitpoints]] '''[[Hitpoints]]''': Represents total life pool. Characters begin at '''Level 10''' (1,154 XP). As Hitpoints levels up, max health increases, allowing survival against heavy attacks.

== Magic Skills ==
Magic in EvilQuest is bifurcated into two distinct mystical arts:

* [[File:Light_Magic.png|21x21px|middle|link=Light Magic|alt=Light Magic]] '''[[Light Magic]]''' (Starts at Lvl 0):
** '''Transmutation''': Transform raw materials into more valuable resources (e.g. transmuting Tin/Copper into Iron, Iron into Silver, Silver into Gold, Logs into Willow/Oak, and Feathers).
** '''Enchanting''': Channel enchantments (Tiers 1–5) to imbue cut gem jewelry into potent accessories: Amulet of Defence, Amulet of Strength, Amulet of Magic, Amulet of Health, and Amulet of Agility.
** '''Utility & Healing''': Restoration of health, cleanses, protective wards, and realm teleports.
* [[File:Dark_Magic.png|21x21px|middle|link=Dark Magic|alt=Dark Magic]] '''[[Dark Magic]]''' (Starts at Lvl 0):
** '''Destructive Spellcasting''': Cast offensive elemental spells like Fire Bolt, scaling in damage with spell tier and magic power.
** '''Curses & Hexes''': Debuff enemy stats, drain life, and inflict lingering damage over time.

== Gathering Skills ==
Gathering skills allow players to harvest raw, unrefined materials directly from the environment:

* [[File:Woodcutting.png|21x21px|middle|link=Woodcutting|alt=Woodcutting]] '''[[Woodcutting]]''': Use axes to fell normal trees, Oak, Willow, Maple, Yew, Magic, and Elder trees. Harvested logs feed into [[Crafting]] (fletching bows/arrows), [[Survival]] (firemaking), and [[Light Magic]] (transmutation).
* [[File:Mining.png|21x21px|middle|link=Mining|alt=Mining]] '''[[Mining]]''': Use pickaxes to harvest ores from mineral rocks across mines and caves (Tin, Copper, Iron, Coal, Silver, Gold, Mithril, Adamantite, Runite, Crimsonite), as well as uncut gems (Sapphire, Emerald, Ruby, Diamond).
* [[File:Fishing.png|21x21px|middle|link=Fishing|alt=Fishing]] '''[[Fishing]]''': Gather aquatic food supplies using fishing rods, bait, and harpoons along rivers, lakes, and oceans. Catches can be cooked to restore health.

== Artisan Skills ==
Artisan skills refine gathered raw resources into usable equipment, consumables, and gear:

* [[File:Smithing.png|21x21px|middle|link=Smithing|alt=Smithing]] '''[[Smithing]]''': Use furnaces to smelt ores and coal into metal bars (Bronze, Iron, Steel, Mithril, Adamantite, Runite, Crimsonite) and anvils to forge metal armor, weaponry, and ammunition heads.
* [[File:Cooking.png|21x21px|middle|link=Cooking|alt=Cooking]] '''[[Cooking]]''': Prepare nourishing meals at ranges and campfires to restore Hitpoints. Cooking also encompasses '''Herbal Tea Brewing''' (21 unique tea recipes across 7 tea leaf types brewed with secondary ingredients), which grant lingering Health Regeneration over time (up to 300s), Maximum Health Boosts, and skill buffs.
* [[File:Crafting.png|21x21px|middle|link=Crafting|alt=Crafting]] '''[[Crafting]]''': An expansive trade encompassing:
** ''Leatherworking & Tanning'': Tan raw hides into leather and dragonhide (Green, Blue, Red, Black), then craft armor pieces.
** ''Gem Cutting'': Cut raw gems with a chisel for jewelry crafting.
** ''Fletching'': Carve logs into unstrung bows and combine them with bowstrings; affix feathers and arrowheads onto headless arrows.
** ''Vorass Weaponry'': Forge specialized Vorass-tier armaments from rare creature remnants.

== Support Skills ==
Support skills provide utility, mobility, stealth, and survival capabilities:

* [[File:Roguery.png|21x21px|middle|link=Roguery|alt=Roguery]] '''[[Roguery]]''': The art of thievery, lockpicking, and subterfuge. Used to open locked rogue chests found throughout dungeons and wilderness zones, yielding coins, rare gems, and magical relics.
* [[File:Survival.png|21x21px|middle|link=Survival|alt=Survival]] '''[[Survival]]''': Wilderness survival and firemaking. Use tinderboxes with logs to create fires for cooking in the field and staying warm, as well as foraging wild flora.
* [[File:Agility.png|21x21px|middle|link=Agility|alt=Agility]] '''[[Agility]]''': Enhances mobility and enables traversal of 15 obstacle courses and world shortcuts (e.g. crawl pipes, balancing logs, tightropes, rock climbs, and stepping stones), significantly reducing travel times between key locations.

